meta {
  name: Milestones
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/method/implementor.client_api.get_milestones?project=PROJ-0029
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  project: PROJ-0029
  ~customer: Hamza
}

tests {
  test("returns 200", function () {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("has message", function () {
    expect(res.body).to.have.property("message");
  });

  test("has counts and a display_state per milestone", function () {
    const m = res.body.message;
    expect(m.total).to.equal(m.milestones.length);
    m.milestones.forEach(function (x) {
      expect(x).to.have.property("id");
      expect(x).to.have.property("completed_on");
      if (x.status !== "completed") expect(x.completed_on).to.equal(null);
      expect(x.display_state).to.be.oneOf([
        "signed_off", "ready_for_sign_off", "awaiting_admin_sign_off",
        "in_progress", "overdue", "on_hold", "upcoming"
      ]);
    });
  });
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  A project's milestones and sign-off counts. Works for implementation and AMC projects.

  **Endpoint:** `GET /api/method/implementor.client_api.get_milestones`  
  **Screens:** Implementation → Milestones tab, AMC details (payment milestones)

  **Permission:** Signed-in client user (Client User or Client Admin). Only records of the user's own client company are returned.

  **Query parameters:**

  | Field | Type | Required | Example | Notes |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `project` | string | yes | `PROJ-0029` | Project `name`. |
  | `customer` | string | no | `Hamza` | Not used by the app. The server picks the user's company. Disabled by default. |

  **Response:** in order, first milestone first.

  ```json
  {
    "message": {
      "milestones": [
        {
          "id": "s6ri3u6d64",
          "title": "Configuration complete",
          "duration": "14",
          "start_date": "2026-10-01",
          "end_date": "2026-10-15",
          "days_left": null,
          "status": "completed",
          "display_state": "signed_off",
          "completed_on": "2026-10-15T17:42:10+03:00",
          "percent": 100,
          "modules": 3,
          "signed_off": {
            "by": "Hamza Admin",
            "on": "2026-10-28T15:13:48+03:00",
            "remarks": "All good"
          },
          "ready_for_sign_off": false,
          "can_sign_off": false
        }
      ],
      "signed_off": 2,
      "completed": 3,
      "total": 6
    }
  }
  ```

  **Milestone fields:**

  - `id`: send this as `milestone` to Sign off.
  - `title`: milestone name to show.
  - `end_date`: planned date. `start_date` is also given.
  - `duration`: free text as our team typed it (e.g. `"14"`), a **string** or null. Don't do date maths with it.
  - `days_left`: days until `end_date`, negative when past. Null once the milestone is completed, or when there is no `end_date`.
  - `status`: `not_started`, `in_progress`, `partially_completed`, `on_hold`, `due` or `completed`. Null when not set. Don't build the UI from it; use `display_state`.
  - `completed_on`: date-time with offset when `status` became `completed`. Null when the milestone isn't completed. Approximate for milestones completed before 11 Nov 2026 (it was filled from the time the milestone row was last changed).
  - `percent`: completion, 0 to 100 (may be fractional). `modules`: number of modules the milestone covers.
  - `signed_off`: null until signed off. Then `by` (full name), `on` (date-time with offset) and `remarks` (null if none were given).
  - `ready_for_sign_off`: true for everyone when the milestone is waiting for sign-off.
  - `can_sign_off`: true only when ready **and** the user is a Client Admin. Show the Sign off button only when this is true.

  **`display_state`: one value per milestone, decided by the server:**

  | Value | Show |
  | --- | --- |
  | `signed_off` | Signed off, with `signed_off.by` and date (green) |
  | `ready_for_sign_off` | "Ready for sign-off" with the Sign off button (maroon) |
  | `awaiting_admin_sign_off` | "Awaiting admin sign-off", no button (maroon). Client Users see this. |
  | `in_progress` | In progress (blue) |
  | `overdue` | Overdue: `end_date` has passed and it isn't completed |
  | `on_hold` | On hold (grey) |
  | `upcoming` | Not started yet (grey) |

  **Counts:** `signed_off`, `completed` and `total` are for the header, e.g. "2 of 6 signed off".

  **Which milestones:** only those of the project's contract type. An AMC project returns only its AMC milestones; an implementation returns only its implementation milestones. Milestones from an AMC's implementation phase are never included, so an AMC with no AMC milestone returns an empty list (`total` 0).

  **Errors:** client API errors have an `error_code`; auth errors raised by Frappe don't.

  - **401** (no error_code): token expired or invalid. Refresh once and retry, else sign out.
  - **403** (no error_code): no Authorization header sent.
  - **403** `not_permitted`: not this client's project, or the project doesn't exist.
  - **403** `no_client_linked`: the user isn't linked to any client company.
  - **417** `missing_parameter`: `project` left out.
}
